<template><main class="about-page"><section class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PRODUCT</div><h1>Built for deliberate discovery.</h1><p>INDEX is a portfolio product exploring resilient API-driven interfaces with public cultural data.</p></section><section class="about-grid"><div><span>01 / DATA</span><h2>Real catalogue, not mock content.</h2><p>Search and work detail data come from Open Library. Covers are loaded from its dedicated Covers API, with designed fallbacks for missing artwork.</p></div><div><span>02 / STATE</span><h2>The URL is part of the interface.</h2><p>Query, language, sort and pagination are reflected in route query parameters so searches remain shareable and navigable.</p></div><div><span>03 / RESILIENCE</span><h2>Failure is designed, too.</h2><p>Abortable requests, skeletons, retry states, empty results and missing-image handling are treated as product states, not afterthoughts.</p></div></section></main></template>
